    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 12.941 + 0.578x $10^{-3}$ T - 2.116x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 12.941x $10^{-3}$ T + 0.289x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 2.116x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 4.594</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td>298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -86.587 + 0.261 \\times 10^{-3}T - 0.045 \\times 10^{-6}T^{2} + 76.950T^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td></td><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -86.587 - 0.261 \\times 10^{-3}T \\ln T + 0.045 \\times 10^{-6}T^{2} + 38.475T^{-1} + 16.288 \\times 10^{-3}T$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Pankratz (92). ",
